---
title: Coconut Cream Pie
author: Mildred McKinzie
category: Desserts
cook time: 10 minutes
source: Loving Memories of Mildred
---

@sugar{1%cup}
@flour{0.5%cup}
@salt{0.25%tsp}
@scalded milk{3%cups}
@egg yolks{3}
@butter{2%Tbsp}
@vanilla{1%tsp}
@coconut{0.5%cup}
@baked pie shell{1}
@egg whites{3}
@sugar for meringue{6%Tbsp}
@additional coconut

Mix sugar, flour, and salt. Add to 3 cups scalded milk, stirring constantly for 2 minutes. Beat 3 egg yolks slightly and add small amount of hot mixture to it. Then add it to entire amount and cook for 1 minute, stirring over low heat. Add 2 Tbsp butter and cool slightly. Add 1 tsp vanilla and 1/2 c coconut. Pour into baked pie shell and cool. Beat 3 egg whites till stiff and gradually add 6 Tbsp sugar. Put on pie and sprinkle with additional coconut. Brown in 375 degree oven for 10 minutes. Cool.
